[run.sh] encoder: x264enc (software) @ 8000kbit/s — no /dev/v4l2-nvenc

  ── Publishing detections over MQTT ──────────────────────────
  Broker : localhost:1883
  Topic  : junction/events

  To CHECK messages are arriving — start it BEFORE the pipeline,
  because messages sent while nobody is listening are discarded,
  not queued.

  From this machine (nothing to install):
      docker run --rm --network host --entrypoint mosquitto_sub craftifaidocker/deepstream:7.1-amd64-v3 -h localhost -p 1883 -t 'junction/events' -v

  From any machine that has the mosquitto clients installed:
      mosquitto_sub -h localhost -p 1883 -t 'junction/events' -v

  To USE it, subscribe to that topic from your own program. One
  JSON message per frame: frame number, camera id, timestamp, and
  a list of objects — each with a label, a tracking id that
  follows it between frames, a confidence and a bounding box.

  Change the broker without rebuilding:
      MQTT_HOST=10.0.0.9 ./run.sh
